    "custom_liquid_ekefkB": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "TILE FAQ",
      "settings": {
        "title": "",
        "include_margins": true,
        "liquid": "{%- comment -%}\n  =====================================================================\n  MIRROR FAQ BLOCK  —  paste into a \"Liquid\" block on the mirror template\n  (title field can be left blank; heading is rendered below)\n  Accordion uses native <details> (no JS). FAQPage schema included.\n  Answers are UK-specific and apply across LED mirror SKUs. Edit any\n  model-specific lines (Bluetooth / Tri-Light / demister) per range.\n  =====================================================================\n{%- endcomment -%}\n\n<style>\n  .mfaq{font-family:\"Roboto\",sans-serif;max-width:920px;margin:0 auto}\n  .mfaq__h{font-family:\"Fraunces\",serif;font-weight:700;font-size:34px;line-height:1.15;color:#016FD0;margin:0 0 8px}\n  .mfaq__sub{color:#5a6068;font-size:15px;margin:0 0 22px}\n  .mfaq__item{border:1px solid #e6e8eb;border-radius:12px;margin-bottom:12px;overflow:hidden;background:#fff}\n  .mfaq__item[open]{border-color:#016FD0}\n  .mfaq__q{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;padding:18px 20px;font-size:16px;font-weight:600;color:#1a1d24;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:14px}\n  .mfaq__q::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}\n  .mfaq__q::after{content:\"+\";font-size:22px;font-weight:400;color:#016FD0;flex:0 0 auto;transition:transform .2s}\n  .mfaq__item[open] .mfaq__q::after{transform:rotate(45deg)}\n  .mfaq__a{padding:0 20px 18px;color:#3a4047;font-size:15px;line-height:1.65}\n  .mfaq__a a{color:#016FD0;font-weight:600}\n  @media(max-width:600px){.mfaq__h{font-size:26px}}\n</style>\n\n<section class=\"mfaq\">\n  <h2 class=\"mfaq__h\">LED Mirror FAQs</h2>\n  <p class=\"mfaq__sub\">Everything you need to know before you buy &amp; fit your mirror.</p>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Are LED bathroom mirrors safe to use in a bathroom?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">Yes. Our LED mirrors are <strong>IP44 rated</strong>, meaning they're protected against splashing water from any direction. Under UK wiring regulations (BS 7671) that makes them suitable for Zone 2 — the area around a basin — and any zone beyond it.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Which bathroom zone can I install it in?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">An IP44 rating covers <strong>Zone 2 and outside zones</strong> — typically above a basin or on any wall away from direct shower spray. For Zone 1 (directly above a bath or shower), an IP65 fitting is recommended. If you're unsure, position the mirror at least 60cm from the bath or shower edge.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Do I need an electrician to fit it?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">If the mirror is hardwired into the mains, yes — bathroom electrical work in the UK falls under <strong>Part P Building Regulations</strong> and should be carried out by a qualified electrician on an RCD-protected circuit. Always check the supplied instructions for your specific model.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Does the demister keep the whole mirror clear?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">The heated demister pad sits behind the glass and keeps a generous central area clear — more than enough to shave or apply makeup straight after a hot shower. Give it a minute or two after switching on to reach full effect.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">What's the difference between front-lit and backlit?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\"><strong>Front-lit</strong> mirrors throw light forward onto your face — the best choice for detailed tasks like makeup and shaving. <strong>Backlit</strong> mirrors cast a soft glow around the edges for a calmer, more ambient, spa-like feel. Some designs combine both.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Can I mount it portrait or landscape?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">Yes — our mirrors are designed for both <strong>vertical and horizontal</strong> mounting, so they'll suit your space either way. Check the position of the touch control before fixing so it ends up where you want it.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Can I change the light colour?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">Tri-Light models let you cycle between <strong>warm, neutral and cool white</strong> with a tap of the touch sensor, and a memory function remembers your last setting — cool light to wake up, warmer light to wind down.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">How does the Bluetooth work?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">On Bluetooth models, pair your phone or tablet to the mirror's built-in speaker to play music or podcasts while you get ready — no extra gadgets or wiring needed.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">Is the glass safe?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">Our mirrors use <strong>copper-free, shatter-resistant glass</strong>, which resists the black-edge corrosion common in steamy bathrooms and is safer if accidentally knocked.</div>\n  </details>\n\n  <details class=\"mfaq__item\">\n    <summary class=\"mfaq__q\">How long do the LEDs last and how much do they cost to run?</summary>\n    <div class=\"mfaq__a\">The LEDs are rated for around <strong>50,000 hours</strong> and draw very little power, so they're cheap to run and you won't be replacing anything for years.</div>\n  </details>\n</section>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n  \"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n  \"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n  \"mainEntity\": [\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Are LED bathroom mirrors safe to use in a bathroom?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes. Our LED mirrors are IP44 rated, meaning they are protected against splashing water from any direction. Under UK wiring regulations (BS 7671) that makes them suitable for Zone 2 around a basin and any zone beyond it.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Which bathroom zone can I install an LED mirror in?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"An IP44 rating covers Zone 2 and outside zones, typically above a basin or on any wall away from direct shower spray. For Zone 1 directly above a bath or shower, an IP65 fitting is recommended. If unsure, position the mirror at least 60cm from the bath or shower edge.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Do I need an electrician to fit an LED mirror?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"If the mirror is hardwired into the mains, yes. Bathroom electrical work in the UK falls under Part P Building Regulations and should be carried out by a qualified electrician on an RCD-protected circuit.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Does the demister keep the whole mirror clear?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The heated demister pad sits behind the glass and keeps a generous central area clear, more than enough to shave or apply makeup straight after a hot shower. Allow a minute or two after switching on to reach full effect.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"What is the difference between front-lit and backlit LED mirrors?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Front-lit mirrors throw light forward onto your face, best for makeup and shaving. Backlit mirrors cast a soft glow around the edges for a calmer, more ambient feel. Some designs combine both.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I mount the mirror portrait or landscape?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Yes, our mirrors are designed for both vertical and horizontal mounting. Check the position of the touch control before fixing so it ends up where you want it.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Can I change the light colour?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Tri-Light models let you cycle between warm, neutral and cool white with the touch sensor, and a memory function remembers your last setting.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How does the Bluetooth work?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"On Bluetooth models, pair your phone or tablet to the mirror's built-in speaker to play music or podcasts while you get ready.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"Is the glass safe?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"Our mirrors use copper-free, shatter-resistant glass, which resists black-edge corrosion in steamy bathrooms and is safer if accidentally knocked.\"}},\n    {\"@type\":\"Question\",\"name\":\"How long do the LEDs last and how much do they cost to run?\",\"acceptedAnswer\":{\"@type\":\"Answer\",\"text\":\"The LEDs are rated for around 50,000 hours and draw very little power, so they are cheap to run and will not need replacing for years.\"}}\n  ]\n}\n</script>"
      }
    },
